{
  "_comment": [
    "Differential conformance input for the grammar-4 operators. The recording",
    "path cannot reach these: its deny-case mutators have no way to violate a",
    "scaled bound, and they skip `or` entirely because violating one branch",
    "proves nothing while another can still permit.",
    "",
    "The predicate is a swap policy that exercises all of v4 at once:",
    "  and(",
    "    or(call_fn == swap_a, call_fn == swap_b),   <- disjunction",
    "    call_arg(1) >= call_arg(0) * 99/100,        <- scaled floor, gte",
    "    call_arg(2) < 1000,                         <- strict lt",
    "    call_arg(3) > 5                             <- strict gt",
    "  )",
    "",
    "Cases sit ON the bounds wherever a bound exists, because that is where a",
    "strictness bug hides: lt/lte and gt/gte differ only at the bound, and a",
    "case one unit away from it passes under either."
  ],
  "predicate": {
    "op": "and",
    "children": [
      {
        "op": "or",
        "children": [
          {
            "op": "eq",
            "left": { "kind": "call_fn" },
            "right": { "kind": "literal_symbol", "value": "swap_a" }
          },
          {
            "op": "eq",
            "left": { "kind": "call_fn" },
            "right": { "kind": "literal_symbol", "value": "swap_b" }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "op": "gte",
        "left": { "kind": "call_arg", "index": 1 },
        "right": { "kind": "call_arg_scaled", "index": 0, "num": "99", "den": "100" }
      },
      {
        "op": "lt",
        "left": { "kind": "call_arg", "index": 2 },
        "right": { "kind": "literal_i128", "value": "1000" }
      },
      {
        "op": "gt",
        "left": { "kind": "call_arg", "index": 3 },
        "right": { "kind": "literal_i128", "value": "5" }
      }
    ]
  },
  "cases": [
